  },
  "articleBody": "It's frustrating when you fix trim only for the damage to reappear, isn't it? Often, the root cause isn't addressed, leading to recurring issues. We often see damage from water intrusion, especially around windows, doors, and the roofline. If your gutters are clogged or downspouts aren't directing water away from your home in areas like Denver or Aurora, that moisture can seep into your trim. Another big culprit is simply old, worn-out paint and caulk that no longer protect the wood from the elements. Pests can also cause surprising damage that looks similar to rot. When we assess trim, we don't just look at the visibly damaged spot; we inspect the surrounding areas, checking corners, seams, and even your home's substrate for hidden moisture. Knowing *why* the damage happened is crucial for a lasting repair. Sometimes it's a simple fix like clearing a gutter, other times it might involve a more comprehensive repair to prevent future headaches. Understanding the cause helps us recommend the best solution to make your home feel more like a home again.",
